From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Il tuo nome <tu@esempio.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Say that re-enabling Ethernet needs a full
 power-down

The LAN disable bit of the W541 Ethernet switch is in the SUS well,
which a reset and standby keep, so clearing it does not bring the
controller back: on a ThinkPad W541 with the option turned off and then
on, a cold boot cleared the bit but the GbE stayed absent ("PCI: Static
device PCI: 00:00:19.0 not found"), as only a G3 (the power removed)
resets the SUS well. Say so in the help text, where it claimed the next
boot alone brings it back.

TEST=tools/cfr-dump.sh of ouroBIOS on the W541 build: 28028 bytes.

Change-Id: I7f01c3c777d112141961fbbd6ed60ce94c0d033d
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 4756ebe2ea..5ecef9db3d 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -745,12 +745,10 @@ static const struct sm_object onboard_ethernet = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.ui_name	= "Ethernet",
 	.ui_helptext	= "The Gigabit Ethernet controller (Intel I217-LM).\n"
 			  "Default: on. Off: the controller is turned off in the\n"
-			  "chipset, for every OS and for network boot. A change takes\n"
-			  "effect with one extra restart, done by the firmware at the\n"
-			  "next boot (the memory may be trained again then). The\n"
-			  "setting is kept in the chipset: a firmware version without\n"
-			  "this option leaves the Ethernet as it was until it is\n"
-			  "turned on here again or the CMOS battery is removed.",
+			  "chipset, for every OS and for network boot, with one extra\n"
+			  "restart. The bit is in a part of the chipset that a reset\n"
+			  "and standby keep, so turning Ethernet back on needs a full\n"
+			  "power-down (the adapter and the battery out for a moment).",
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
